{
  "version": "2026-07-31.1",
  "_about": [
    "NOVARA built-in save-location knowledge base. Compiled into the binary via",
    "include_str!, so a fresh offline install detects saves for common titles on",
    "first launch.",
    "",
    "TWO KINDS OF ENTRY.",
    "",
    "1. Convention rules (match_kind = 'any', priority 100). These describe ENGINE",
    "   and OPERATING SYSTEM conventions, not launcher conventions -- Steam, GOG and",
    "   Epic impose almost no save-location convention on what they distribute. A",
    "   convention rule is safe to apply to every game because a candidate is only",
    "   produced when the expanded path actually exists, so one Unreal rule covers",
    "   every Unreal game without NOVARA knowing which games use Unreal.",
    "",
    "2. Curated titles (match_kind = 'title_norm', priority 10). Lower priority",
    "   number wins, so a curated entry outranks a convention rule.",
    "",
    "PROVENANCE. Every curated entry carries source_ref 'curated:phase1'. These come",
    "from the author's own familiarity with these games, NOT from PCGamingWiki,",
    "Ludusavi or any other dataset -- none were consulted, and importing one requires",
    "a licence review first (see KNOWLEDGE_BASE.md 9).",
    "",
    "VALIDATION (task 1.22). Probed against a real machine's filesystem. Result:",
    "  - CONFIRMED: builtin:elden-ring resolved a real {WILDCARD} account directory,",
    "    validating wildcard expansion end to end on real data.",
    "  - CORRECTED: red-dead-redemption-2. The game folder existed but Profiles/ did",
    "    not, so the entry contributed nothing on an installed game. A parent-level",
    "    fallback was ADDED at lower precedence rather than replacing the precise",
    "    entry -- both are correct, and the precise one still wins when it resolves.",
    "    The same fallback was added for GTA V, whose vendor folder was confirmed.",
    "  - INCONCLUSIVE: the remaining 27. Their games are not installed on the test",
    "    machine, so a miss says nothing about the path. Entries carrying",
    "    source_ref 'curated:phase1' remain UNVERIFIED.",
    "  Nothing was removed. A miss with no evidence is not grounds for deletion.",
    "",
    "WHEN UNSURE, OMIT. A wrong entry is worse than a missing one: the Write Witness",
    "(Phase 2) will find what the KB misses, but a wrong path can be bound and",
    "restored into. Two rules followed here: no path was guessed, and where the exact",
    "subfolder was uncertain the PARENT directory was used instead (Terraria, for",
    "example, keeps saves in both Players/ and Worlds/, so the entry names Terraria/).",
    "",
    "NOT EXPRESSIBLE YET. Steam Cloud's <Steam install>/userdata/<id>/<appid>/remote",
    "is the one genuine launcher convention, and the template variable set has no",
    "anchor for the Steam installation directory. Inventing one that resolved to a",
    "guessed path would be worse than omitting the rule.",
    "",
    "match_value for title_norm must be pre-normalised: lowercase, all",
    "non-alphanumerics removed (KNOWLEDGE_BASE.md 4.1). Validation rejects anything",
    "else rather than repairing it."
  ],

  "entries": [
